course: dictionary
lesson: 3741
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «flounder» is one of them. Read the whole sentence first, then ask which meaning fits the clues around the word.
explain: «A flounder lies flat on the seabed, flicks sand over its edges.» Here a flounder is an animal, a flat sea fish. The clues are seabed and sand. Try the other meaning in the sentence and it makes no sense.
explain: «The gentlemen and the driver flounder in the pond in their long coats.» Now flounder is an action word. The clues are pond and long coats: they are struggling to move, splashing and stumbling in the water. Ask yourself: what are they doing?
explain: A third meaning is about the mind. If a pupil begins to flounder in a test, she is stuck and does not know what to write or say. The clue is the test itself, not water or mud.
fact: «Flounder» can be a noun: a flat sea fish that lies on the seabed, with both eyes on one side of its head.
fact: As a verb, «flounder» means to struggle to move, splashing and stumbling, as in deep mud, snow or water.
fact: «Flounder» can also mean to struggle and not know what to say or do, as in a test.
fact: Useful phrases are «flounder about», «flounder in» and «begin to flounder».
fact: Camouflage helps a flounder hide: it changes its colour and pattern to match the sandy seabed.
exercise: «A flounder lies flat on the seabed.» What is a flounder here? | A sort of wave | *A flat sea fish | A pair of boots | A bird that sings
exercise: «Toad lands on his back and begins to flounder in the pond.» What does flounder mean here? | *To struggle to move, splashing and stumbling | To fly high in the sky | To sleep in the soft grass | To sing loudly
exercise: Priya says, «I began to flounder in the maths test.» What does she mean? | She was swimming very fast | *She was stuck and did not know what to do | She was eating a fish for lunch | She solved every question quickly
test: «The flounder changed its colour to match the sand.» What is a flounder in this sentence? | A kind of thick mud | *A flat sea fish | A school desk | A bird that nests in trees
test: «The walkers floundered in the deep snow.» What does floundered mean? | Ran very fast | *Struggled to move, stumbling | Found a treasure chest | Slept soundly
exam: «After the long question he began to flounder, unsure what to write.» What does flounder mean here? | Hide under the desk | Swim up to the surface | *Struggle and not know what to do | Smile happily at the teacher
